  "prompt": "Build an original Kanban Board in plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript without runtime dependencies. Move complete task cards among three columns. Placeholders reflow from their current positions, counts update on drop, and keyboard lifting supports the same moves. Match Figma Stage 145:1591 and all 24 native layers, 1 supplied SVG slots and 0 exact approved v2 photo slots. Keep unchanged SVG bytes, root dimensions and offsets, original reference copy, the complete full model and local datasets. Native retains its exact 372×264 reference composition inside the shared fitted Stage; full uses a 640×520 plane. The shell owns replay, pause and outer chrome. Preserve native keyboard/touch, independent caller/document/viewport holds, queued intent, interruption, capture cleanup, reduced 150ms inert old-paint fades, at least 11px rendered type and complete portable exports. Photo previews retain original approved 800/1600px hashes and attribution; portable exports use the licensed 800px files. Pro candidates stay free until the owner chooses the seams flag. Preserve all 24 native layers: three 94×160 columns at (38,30), (140,30), (242,30), five native cards, the [3,3] dashed placeholder and lifted centre card at (150,66), plus the unchanged cursor. Full retains nine unique tasks: Define the interaction, Match the native layout, Complete keyboard navigation; Refine the motion curves, Verify mouse and touch, Write the complete prompt; Run the browser stories, Publish the verified phase, Check the offline export. Keep committed counts until drop, keyed card DOM, measured 350ms FLIP from current poses, real placeholders, stable ancestor pointer capture, and complete rollback on cancel. Space lifts, Arrow keys choose a column or slot, Enter drops, Escape cancels. Native input exposes every task through three scrollable columns with short labels and complete accessible titles."
